        "text": "Beware, cheap and racist mentality of security armed guards at temple. I took photo at around 5.45 pm today 19 August and a guard at the door barked and then when I went inside the main door to temple he was standing on left side with a gun he asked me for the phone and then went into delete photos even though they were taken outside. Then when I tried to take my phone back he stared at his gun and then me to scare me, he then shouted this is Nepal, many times and that I need to remember that. Very disgusting behaviour inside main temple, they are the ones disrespecting people coming to the temple. The similar photo he deleted is attached I retook it as everyone (locals) was taking it here. Also I would say to the foreign tourists don't buy 1000 NPR tickets, it's just not worth it as if your not Hindu they won't let you in the main temple even after paying that much. That's the main thing to see the UNESCO historical building! There is nothing else to see! They don't deserve your financial support.",
